#. module: stock_account_multicompany_ux
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:stock_account_multicompany_ux.field_product_category__shared_to_branches
msgid ""
"For a parent company that keeps the stock and the purchases while its branches only invoice (for example, a branch to invoice in B). The branches take the costing method, valuation and accounts of the parent, cannot change them, and their invoices take the cost of goods sold at the parent's cost.\n"
"\n"
"It does not apply when the branches have their own warehouses: their stock moves would be valued at each branch's own cost.\n"
"\n"
"This flag is company-dependent: it is edited on the group's root company and synced down to its branches, so each company group can decide independently which categories are shared."
msgstr ""

